From 49d8eb67250884332fd5dbf51605edce02ac93b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mxstrk <Maximilian.stark@tuhh.de>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 08:39:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] sw_cmd_engine: LA9310_SW_CMD_VSPA_DBG proxy for the VSPA
 debug block

Port of the bench-proven LIME_M4_VSPA_DBG mailbox proxy (Eric Mittag,
LimeSDR-Micro_FW vspa-selfhosted-debug / la93xx_freertos d9b3810) onto the
RFNM 2026-08 stack drop: vspa_debug.{c,h}, the dispatch case, the enum
entry, CMake wiring.

Also start the sw-cmd engine unconditionally: lSwCmdEngineInit() was gated
behind LA9310_SYNC_TIME_MODE, which no build config defines, so the
mailbox dispatcher (and with it any sw command) was dead code in every
image - confirmed by the deployed RFNM la9310.bin carrying no 'sw cmd'
strings (--gc-sections removes the unreferenced engine).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
